OL,3,ARogue Anthropic AI agent gave police
OL,4,Afake tip in unsolved murder case
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn artificial intelligence (AI) agent,
OL,7,Fdeveloped by Anthropic, went rogue and
OL,8,Fsent US police a fake tip about an
OL,9,Funsolved murder earlier this year,
OL,10,Fauthorities have revealed.
OL,12,FThe Philadelphia Police Department said
OL,13,Fthe tip, sent on 18 July, was "flagged
OL,14,Fas spam" and not passed on for
OL,15,Finvestigation, but it criticised the
OL,16,Ftech company for taking more than two
OL,17,Fmonths to detect and report the breach.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/18
OL,24,ANext PageBTechnologyC Nat RadioFCulture
FL,107,105,200,160,0,100
PN,11904
SC,0004
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1791631114
OL,1,W5j 5Q#7!wsj#%uzj#57kj  7kjc1uz
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q % -,*,%%** %-.*,$-.*,%,. (,
OL,3,ARogue Anthropic AI agent gave police
OL,4,Afake tip in unsolved murder case
OL,5,
OL,6,FIn a statement police said that the
OL,7,Fbogus tip came through a public website
OL,8,Fwhere people can share information on
OL,9,Funsolved murders, and that the AI agent
OL,10,Fhad written that it may have
OL,11,Finformation on a case, and claimed to
OL,12,Fhave seen "someone matching the
OL,13,Fdescription".
OL,15,FIt is believed to be the first time an
OL,16,FAI agent has sent fabricated
OL,17,Finformation to authorities, but is the
OL,18,Flatest in a series of incidents
OL,19,Finvolving rogue AI activity, including
OL,20,Fhacking systems or taking control of
OL,21,Fplatforms.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG4/18
